# Snakemake Pipeline for *Ampullaceana balthica* Gut Microbiome Study

This plan creates a two-phase Snakemake pipeline that replicates the `R_temporaria_Metagenomics`
shell pipeline for the *Ampullaceana balthica* 16S rRNA amplicon study. The pipeline is split
into two phases because two steps require manual inspection of visualization outputs before
parameters can be set.

**Current state:** Raw demultiplexed [.qza](file:///c:/Users/Utilizador/OneDrive%20-%20Instituto%20Polit%C3%A9cnico%20de%20Set%C3%BAbal/Documents/Bioinformatica/Est%C3%A1gio/Ampullaceana%20balthica/ampullaceana_demux.qza) artifact ([ampullaceana_demux.qza](file:///c:/Users/Utilizador/OneDrive%20-%20Instituto%20Polit%C3%A9cnico%20de%20Set%C3%BAbal/Documents/Bioinformatica/Est%C3%A1gio/Ampullaceana%20balthica/ampullaceana_demux.qza)) already exists.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Two manual checkpoints exist where you must inspect QIIME2 visualizations and update `config.yaml` before proceeding:**
> 1. **After Phase 1, Step 1** (demux viz) → set `trunc_f` / `trunc_r` in `config.yaml`
> 2. **After Phase 1, Step 4** (alpha rarefaction curve) → set `raref_depth` in `config.yaml`

> [!NOTE]
> The pipeline will be written for **Linux/HPC** (where QIIME2 runs), not Windows — since QIIME2 does not run natively on Windows. You run it from your Linux server/HPC where the data lives. The [manifest.tsv](file:///c:/Users/Utilizador/OneDrive%20-%20Instituto%20Polit%C3%A9cnico%20de%20Set%C3%BAbal/Documents/Bioinformatica/Est%C3%A1gio/Ampullaceana%20balthica/manifest.tsv) already uses Linux paths (`/home/rmoura/...`), confirming this.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Project root: `Ampullaceana balthica/`

All new files go inside the *Ampullaceana balthica* project directory.

---

#### [NEW] [config.yaml](file:///c:/Users/Utilizador/OneDrive%20-%20Instituto%20Polit%C3%A9cnico%20de%20Set%C3%BAbal/Documents/Bioinformatica/Est%C3%A1gio/Ampullaceana%20balthica/config.yaml)

Central configuration file. Parameters mirror the [R_temporaria_Metagenomics/ConfigFile.yml](file:///c:/Users/Utilizador/OneDrive%20-%20Instituto%20Polit%C3%A9cnico%20de%20Set%C3%BAbal/Documents/Bioinformatica/Est%C3%A1gio/R_temporaria_Metagenomics/ConfigFile.yml) but adapted for this species. You only edit this file between runs.

Key sections:
- `raw`: paths, metadata, manifest, threads
- `illumina`: primers (`515F`/`806R` or similar — **needs confirmation from you**)
- `denoise`: truncation params (left empty until you inspect demux viz)
- `tables`, `taxonomy`, `discriminants`, `diversity`: same as before but for *A. balthica*

