## Verification Plan

### Automated / Dry-run Tests

Snakemake has a built-in dry-run mode that validates the entire DAG without executing any jobs.

**Phase 1 dry-run:**
```bash
conda activate qiime2-amplicon-2024.10
snakemake -s Snakefile_phase1 --configfile config.yaml -n --dag
```
Expected: prints DAG of jobs with no errors.

**Phase 2 dry-run:**
```bash
snakemake -s Snakefile_phase2 --configfile config.yaml -n --dag
```
Expected: prints DAG of jobs with no errors.

### Manual Verification
1. After dry-run passes: run Phase 1 on a **subset of 5–10 samples** first by adding `--config test_samples=True` (we will add a test mode to the config).
2. Inspect [demux.qzv](file:///c:/Users/Utilizador/OneDrive%20-%20Instituto%20Polit%C3%A9cnico%20de%20Set%C3%BAbal/Documents/Bioinformatica/Est%C3%A1gio/Ampullaceana%20balthica/ampullaceana_demux.qzv) at [view.qiime2.org](https://view.qiime2.org), update `config.yaml` with truncation values.
3. Run Phase 1 fully, then inspect alpha rarefaction curve, update `raref_depth`.
4. Run Phase 2 fully.
